**Stackorder commands**

Post a command on a line of its own in a pull request comment. Stack keys are repository relative paths such as `stacks/prod/vpc`, with `:instance` appended to name one instance of the directory; without keys a command covers every affected stack.

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `stackorder plan [stack…]` | Re-plan every affected stack, or only the named ones |
| `stackorder apply [stack…]` | Apply the planned stacks wave by wave; a named subset still honours dependency order |
| `stackorder unlock [stack…]` | Release the orchestration locks this pull request holds (write permission required) |
| `stackorder help` | Show this list of commands |

Lines inside code blocks and quoted replies are ignored.
